		<node type="event_simple" id="5" tag="">
			<journal_entry>Now that you found a $[Resource.L.r_laboratory_NameSingular] and interacted with it, double-click on the $[Skill.A.s_alchemy_NameSingular] icon, and find the $[Resource.P.r_potion_health_minor_NameSingular] recipe icon. Double-click on the $[Resource.P.r_potion_health_minor_NameSingular] and check the required materials list. In some cases, you may need to scroll down the list. Once you have the required materials in your backpack, select to craft one item and click on the large checkmark. In case the crafting fails, you might need to try again - in this case you will need some more materials again.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="interact_with_object" id="0" value="1" tag="An Interact With Object Task" resource_name="r_Laboratory">
					<task_instruction>Find and Interact with a $[Resource.L.r_laboratory_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="6" tag="">
			<journal_entry>Now that you have crafted one $[Resource.P.r_potion_health_minor_NameSingular], it should have been placed in your backpack. If you are able to use one, do so and notice how it affects your character in the System chat tab as well as any notification messages in your user interface.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="craft_item" id="1" value="1" tag="A Craft Item(s) Task" resource_name="r_Potion Health Minor" quantity="1">
					<task_instruction>Craft one $[Resource.P.r_potion_health_minor_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="7" tag="">
			<journal_entry>Now that you saw the effects of  $[Resource.P.r_potion_health_minor_NameSingular], here is one for free!</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="activate_item" id="2" value="1" tag="An Activate Item Task" resource_name="r_Potion Health Minor" consume="False">
					<task_instruction>Use a $[Resource.P.r_potion_health_minor_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
		</node>
